<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.1.13.2.1"/>
    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Two-week follow-up of exertional chest tightness, seen the same day by cardiology after coronary CT angiography. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Shackleton returns two weeks after his first visit, on the day of his cardiology consultation with Dr. Solberg-Adebayo, after coronary CT angiography and an echocardiogram this morning. He stopped smoking on his quit date a week ago and is taking varenicline, with mild nausea after the morning dose that eases with food. The chest tightness comes less often on metoprolol, but still comes two or three times a week on the stairs to his office or when he carries a load, and passes within three minutes of rest. He used nitroglycerin twice, with relief within two minutes. He has had no pain at rest, fainting, or palpitations. He is taking aspirin and atorvastatin every day. He has cut down to two drinks on most evenings. He wanted to know whether any of this would be reported to the expedition&apos;s backers; he was told it would not, without his consent. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Angina</td><td>Two or three episodes a week with stairs or loads; relieved by rest</td></tr><tr><td>Nitroglycerin</td><td>Used twice, effective</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Not smoked for a week; varenicline with mild nausea</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>Two drinks on most evenings</td></tr><tr><td>Red flags</td><td>No rest pain, fainting, or palpitations</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
